  "facts": [
    "The Haliç Bridge, also called the Golden Horn Bridge, opened its lanes on 10 September 1974, linking Istanbul’s inner beltway to the bustling Golden Horn waterfront.",
    "Engineered by Japan’s IHI Corporation and Germany’s Julius Berger-Bauboag AG, the 995‑meter span was completed in just three years, from 1971 to 1974.",
    "Standing 22 meters above sea level, the 32‑meter‑wide bridge carries the O‑1 motorway, a vital artery of Istanbul’s Inner Beltway."
